From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:57:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the UART2 and UART4
 controllers

Boards bring out more A733 UARTs than the console UART0 on their pin
headers, but the SoC dtsi only describes UART0.

Add UART2 at 0x02502000 and UART4 at 0x02504000, both DesignWare APB
UARTs like UART0, with their bus clocks and resets. On the A733 the
UARTs are 4 KiB apart. Add the pin groups that reach the Cubie A7S
headers: UART2 on PB0/PB1 with RTS on PB2 (header J11) and CTS on PB3
(header J6), function 2, and UART4 on PJ24/PJ25 (J11, function 4). Both
nodes are disabled and the pin groups are /omit-if-no-ref/, because
nothing fitted on the board uses them; a board enables what it uses.

Not covered: DMA requests, and the other UARTs.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards with both nodes enabled in
a copy of the DTB; both UARTs probe as 16550A and take PB0/PB1 and
PJ24/PJ25.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 43 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index ae8a7a4d2c61..b9e7035b71dd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -325,6 +325,27 @@ uart0_pb_pins: uart0-pb-pins {
 				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
 				function = "uart0";
 			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			uart2_pb_pins: uart2-pb-pins {
+				pins = "PB0", "PB1";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
+				function = "uart2";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			uart2_rts_cts_pb_pins: uart2-rts-cts-pb-pins {
+				pins = "PB2", "PB3";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
+				function = "uart2";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			uart4_pj_pins: uart4-pj-pins {
+				pins = "PJ24", "PJ25";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <4>;
+				function = "uart4";
+			};
 		};
 
 		ccu: clock-controller@2002000 {
@@ -369,6 +390,28 @@ uart0: serial@2500000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		uart2: serial@2502000 {
+			compatible = "snps,dw-apb-uart";
+			reg = <0x02502000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 4 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			reg-shift = <2>;
+			reg-io-width = <4>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_UART2>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_UART2>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		uart4: serial@2504000 {
+			compatible = "snps,dw-apb-uart";
+			reg = <0x02504000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 6 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			reg-shift = <2>;
+			reg-io-width = <4>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_UART4>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_UART4>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		gic: interrupt-controller@3400000 {
 			compatible = "arm,gic-v3";
 			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
